  "content": {
    "text": "2 days ago\nDow turns red. Microsoft's stock is the biggest drag despite tech's rally.\nThe Dow reversed early gains to slip into negative territory. Ironically, the biggest drag on the Dow was Microsoft's stock, even as the tech sector was seeing a broad bounce.\nThe Dow was up as much as 410 points at its intraday high, reached soon after the open, but was recently down 54 points, or 0.1%. Microsoft's stock was falling $7.73, or 1.9%, to shave about 48 points off the Dow's price.\nMeanwhile, the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite was still rising 1.1%, but pared earlier gains of as much as 1.8%.",
